#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Street Legends frontend: Pharmacies on REAL OpenStreetMap locations.

Mirrors the Activity Centers v2 pattern (real OSM locations, no seeded
fallback) and the Fiend frontend patterns (paren-depth batch discovery,
brace-scan color/icon edits, literal emoji only).

What it adds:
  1. services/api.ts: getPharmaciesNearby + pharmacyBuy + pharmacySell
     (count-guarded per function). Buy/sell POST {player_id, item_id,
     qty, request_id}; a fresh client-side request_id (Date.now +
     random) is generated when the caller does not pass one — the
     backend returns the stored result for a duplicate request_id
     without re-charging, so this is the double-tap backstop.
  2. hooks/useMapQueries.ts: getPharmaciesNearby appended LAST in the
     entity batch (index discovered live with the fiend-followup
     paren-depth parser, so existing results indices never move),
     pharmacies field on MapEntitiesData. Wrapped in withTimeout(...)
     when the entities-fast helper is present, bare otherwise.
  3. app/(tabs)/index.tsx: 'pharmacy' marker type, nearbyPharmacies
     memo, mapMarkers spread + deps, handleMarkerPress branch + deps,
     popup with ENTER only (plus the popup's built-in close X), ENTER
     opens a full-screen Modal on the lab picture (embedded below as a
     data URI; the GitHub push tool cannot carry binary files) with a
     BUY/SELL shop for the five items. No presence/who's-inside list.
     Does NOT touch character.tsx (no SELL buttons re-added), the Fiend
     code, the once-only logic, or the activity-center code.
  4. components/GameMap.tsx: 'pharmacy' in the marker type union,
     markerColors pharmacy '#009688' (teal), markerIcons pharmacy
     literal pill character (NEVER a unicode escape), a pharmacy marker
     branch mirroring the activityCenter pattern, pharmacy in the
     48x62 location sizing (isLocationMarker). Color/icon edits use a
     brace-count scan, NEVER a negated-brace-star regex on these
     objects (that exact pattern broke the map once: the escapes
     contain a closing brace that ends the match early).

Prices (regular buy / pharmacy sell = 50% less, per oz):
  Grass $100/$50, Pills $200/$100, Rock Candy $300/$150,
  Flake $400/$200, Brown Sugar $500/$250.

Run:  python3 frontend/patch-pharmacy-frontend.py
   or:  python3 frontend/patch-pharmacy-frontend.py /path/to/app
Idempotent: rerun prints ALREADY_APPLIED per part, files unchanged.
Frontend / Expo Go only. No build, no Deploy for this patch itself
(the backend patch needs Publish separately).
"""
